From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 22:06:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] WebPlayer: show the web video where the page punches its hole

A page with an opaque background covers the video plane entirely, so
its video stays invisible while it plays. The web engine punches a
transparent hole into such a page where the video element is, and the
video sink reports that rectangle in a RECT message. The layer bridge
scales it from page to screen pixels, fits the video into it by its
display aspect ratio and moves the video plane there, also while no
new frame arrives. Without a rectangle the renderer places the video.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
---
